WEBVTT

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:28.050
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:28.050
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:28.050
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.400 --> 00:02:01.870
The Mutineer
Chapter II

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.730
In August of Imperial Year 482...

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.150
...Reinhard von Musel and Siegfried Kircheis...

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:15.150
...were assigned to their respective
duties on the destroyer, Hameln II.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.520
Well, let's have a drink.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.370
I want to thank you
for saving my little brother.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.240
We have some
treasured brandy.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.310
Hey, Rolf, go get
the usual stuff.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.940
Oh, please don't be square and reproach us for drinking on board, Security Chief.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.040
If it doesn't hinder your duties, I don't plan on disapproving.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.070
But we'll refrain.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.040
Huh ?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.550
So you can't drink
commoners' alcohol ?

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.490
No, that's not it.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.510
I mean...

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.500
...we're underage.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.070
Huh ?

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.390
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:03.720
I'd forgotten about that.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.320
My father manages an urban factory.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:14.320
Since we've been fiddling with machines since we were little, we're good with our hands.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.370
So I went to a technical high school.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.630
And for some unknown reason,
this guy went to art school.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.420
I see.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.490
He may not look like much...

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.840
...but he actually won an award in a national contest in high school for his sculpture.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.430
My little brother is my pride.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.510
Stop that, Brother.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.520
Hey, it's all right,
don't be so modest.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.080
I'm sure he'll be a 
great master someday.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.640
How about it, would you like to buy a few pieces of his work now ?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.050
They'll be worth a lot
a few years from now.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.480
Quit it.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.410
They still come cheap now.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.170
Brother.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.200
I know, I know.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.880
Art is not merchandise, right ?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.980
So even in the military, I requested to be assigned to a technical unit.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.090
I thought if I was lucky, I could work for a rear-line weapon factory...

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.200
...and could retire without 
getting myself killed in battle.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.220
My father's getting up in age, so
I have to take over his factory soon.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.200
But it turned out that I was assigned to be an 
engineer on a destroyer right on front lines.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.810
And for whatever reason, my brother was assigned to the same ship.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.140
Military Personnel may think
they've done us a favor...

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.330
...but if this ship goes down,
we'll both be dead.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.200
Our bereaved, old parents will have no hope left, just get older and die.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.190
Brother, you've drunk too much.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.200
You should...

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.510
It's not just us !

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.450
You remember that skinny kid, Schmitt.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.940
He's a budding scholar who was
studying astrophysics at a university...

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.610
...and he's a fairly intelligent guy.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:53.080
But his draft exemption for general universities ran out, so he had to start as a junior sailor.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:58.490
It's such a shame,
to see such talent wasted.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:03.200
And that guy, Bunto,
he's usually a jokester.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.530
But he never gets letters.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.990
On vacation, he can't go
back to his hometown.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.450
Do you know why ?

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.220
He has no family or friends ?

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.730
That's not it.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.500
He has parents and a sister.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.720
Above it all, he had
just gotten married.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.640
But he left for the military without
telling them that he'd been drafted.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.060
He had to prepare for not being able to return home alive.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.860
So he pretended to just disappear.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.310
That way, even if he dies in battle,
he doesn't have to make his family grieve.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:39.010
If he just disappears, his family can keep on hoping that he might be alive somewhere.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.750
It's a stupid idea, isn't it ?

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.630
That's what I thought, too.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.120
But...

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.040
...I can't laugh at him.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.310
I can't laugh at him !

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.560
Do you see, sir ?

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.930
We sailors, each of us
is a live human being.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:06.740
Each of us has a family, a life, and possibilities for a future.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.000
I want to understand.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:14.540
You officers are in the
position to order us to die.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.320
Battlefields are like that,
so it can't be helped.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.200
But sailors don't want
to die meaninglessly.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.960
They don't want to die
when they don't have to die.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.020
So we want officers to be 
able to make good decisions.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.820
We want officers to be able
to understand the sailors' pain !

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.780
I understand.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.540
I want to know about you guys.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.680
Each one of you.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.350
Are you sure ?

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.800
If you do, it'll be hard for you.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.610
When you order us to die.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.450
That's fine.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.620
Each sailor has a life.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:54.960
With that knowledge, with the understanding of that pain, I'll issue the right orders.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.890
For that sake,
I'd like you to tell me.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.090
You're a more impressive
man than I thought.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.290
All right, I'll tell ya.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:16.110
On September 2nd, Imperial Destroyer Unit 237, including Hameln II...

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:20.490
...advanced nearly 6 light years from Iserlohn Fortress into Free Planets Alliance territory...

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:22.840
...and was about to enter
the Altmuel Star System.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:27.650
The system's star, Altmuel,
is a very unstable red giant...

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.190
...and since the planets in
the system have broken up...

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.080
...and turned into layers of 
asteroids surrounding the star...

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.820
...this space area is known as one of the
most treacherous in the Iserlohn Corridor.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:45.160
Not all the asteroids' orbits have been processed into our data banks.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.040
Don't neglect your
surveillance to the port side.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:47.710
Yes, sir.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.930
Chief Navigator.

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:59.270
Lieutenant Junior Grade,
you don't need to be so tense.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:05.350
You are talented, and I don't know what you think about them, but they are all experts.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:09.740
If you don't leave them to do their routine work, you won't hold up through the long voyage.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.340
Yes, sir.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.750
There's a radar contact off the port side.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.240
Something irregular ?

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.110
I think...

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.410
That's the...

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.450
...enemy !

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:25.940
What ?

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:45.940
Captain !

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:51.720
Call the doctor !

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.300
Assume command, Chief Navigator...

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:57.840
Captain !

00:08:57.840 --> 00:08:58.700
Captain !

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.590
Medical unit, come to 
the bridge immediately.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.500
In accordance with the Captain's
order, I will assume command.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.550
All sections, submit damage reports.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.780
This is bad.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.240
Power generation
has fallen to 40%.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.150
I will go to the engine room.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.390
Please do so.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:18.290
What happened ?

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.070
Oh my god...

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.310
I'll leave him to you.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:26.090
Where's the First Officer ?

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:27.320
I think he'll be here soon, but...

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:28.850
Don't be flustered.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:29.660
Hard to port !

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.490
Did you say port ?

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.000
I will not repeat my orders.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.160
But our allies are all turning to starboard
in an attempt to evacuate from the area...

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.420
Don't make me repeat it !

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.180
Hard to port...

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:50.600
What's happening ?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:55.450
The ship was hit on the lower port side, the Captain was injured due to a secondary explosion...

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.340
...and I am presently in command in
accordance with the Captain's order.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:00.640
We'll take the Captain
to the emergency room.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.680
What's his condition ?

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.030
He's lost consciousness.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.430
It's hard to tell.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.640
The ship's power
output has fallen to 40%...

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.330
...and the Chief Engineer headed
to the engine room for the repairs.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:15.290
Other damage has not been reported.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.320
What's going on ?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.140
Why is our ship
alone and isolated ?

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.130
Under the orders of the
Chief Navigator, we went to port.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.390
LTJG Musel's ?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.080
All right. I'll
take command here.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.230
Turn around and follow our allies !

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.480
Please wait.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.090
This is not a normal battle encounter.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.980
We were taken 
completely by surprise.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:42.750
In other words, the enemy anticipated our
movement and made a fully prepared attack.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:46.770
It's clearly a trap that the enemy's
ranks are thin in the 3 o'clock direction.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.860
That's only speculation.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.740
Since we don't know
the Captain's orders...

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:57.350
...it's only logical to follow our flagship, Kissingen III's, movement regardless of communication status !

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:59.990
Even if there is
no trap at 3 o'clock...

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:03.530
...our ship has suffered damage in the
engine area and can't sustain high speed.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:08.940
If we follow our allies, it's obvious that we'll be immediately feasted on by the enemy ships.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:09.840
Instead...

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:14.050
...we should choose another retreat route while the enemy is pursuing the other four vessels.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.540
Another route ?

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.290
If we proceed to the 9 o'clock
direction as we presently are...

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.680
...there is the body of asteroids
where the enemy was hiding.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.240
We should retreat into that area for the time being to evade enemy pursuit...

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.580
...and finish the
repairs to our ship.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.590
That's insane !

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:30.960
That way, we'll be completely
isolated in enemy territory.

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:35.300
The enemy is comprised mainly
of slow battleships and cruisers.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.940
If the engine is repaired...

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:40.360
...with a destroyer's speed, we can find
a way to break free and lose them.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.510
That's mere armchair theory.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.090
No, no more discussion is necessary.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.610
In any case, I've returned,
so I will take command.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.640
If we follow our allies,
however belatedly...

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.290
...we can receive their support in repairing our ship, also.

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.600
I refuse.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.180
What did you say ?

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.070
I refuse to transfer
command authority.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.280
Nonsense !

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.500
The Captain clearly stated
that he left me in command !

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.450
I will continue in command !

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.770
That's enough !

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:21.060
He named you only because you were the highest ranked officer there at the time !

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:24.590
It's only logical that the First Officer assumes command in the absence of the Captain !

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.580
But the the First Officer's
judgment is not acceptable !

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:33.190
As long as there is a chance of endangering
the ship{if the command were transferred}, I cannot return command authority !

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.520
This is ridiculous.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.340
It doesn't matter.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:38.680
I will take command.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:41.390
Come about, and make
a large arc trajectory...

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.160
...to set a course to
reunite with our allies !

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.530
Command authority
currently lies with me.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.030
Maintain your course.

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.100
Lieutenant Junior Grade Musel !

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:51.730
First Officer !

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.060
Report later !

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:56.060
Ensign Gunaist, if you have
something to report, report it to me.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.100
Lieutenant Junior Grade !

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.860
It doesn't matter who,
please just look !

00:12:58.860 --> 00:12:59.450
Our allies are...

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:03.940
What...?

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:05.190
It's an ambush...

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:06.940
Just as LTJG Musel said...

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.610
The enemy squadron is over 10 ships.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:09.640
Can they escape...?

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.570
Chief Missileer.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:15.240
S...sir ?

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:18.290
I'd like you to discharge a
mine, with a delayed fuse.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:20.400
The explosion needs to be at maximum.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.750
I'd like to camouflage our ship's sinking.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.040
Then we can't do it
with only one mine.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.800
If we detonate three mines simultaneously in proximity, we should be able to manage it.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:33.940
Make it so.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:35.980
Yes, sir.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:40.190
Ensign Gunaist, at the same time as
the mine explosion, turn off the radar.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.000
Huh ?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.070
Don't forget the basics.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.890
Radar emissions will give away
our position to the enemy.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:49.240
Ensign Frebel, only restart
communication monitoring.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:49.720
Yes, sir.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.090
Yes, sir.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.010
The explosion has been confirmed.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:01.420
The radar has been turned off.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:04.060
From now on, monitor
with passive sensors.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:05.390
Put it on speaker.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.040
Activating.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.270
This is Bangendecks...{inaudiblemost likely a name of the ship, sounds something like Bangendecks}.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.340
The ship has suffered a direct hit and is completely crippled.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:11.630
We'll abandon ship...

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:17.080
Bangendecks, Bangendecks, respond !

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.290
{inaudibleanother ship name, sounds like Zinsernein's}...destruction has been confirmed.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.660
Communication with
Bangendecks has been cut off...

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.330
This is Destroyer Unit 237.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.370
We've encountered the enemy inside the Iserlohn Corridor.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:29.110
Kissingen III, Kissin...

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:35.290
All communications have been cut off...

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:39.090
Four explosions have been confirmed through the passive sensors.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:43.490
Based on the yield, they are
presumed to be destroyer class...

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.520
It is just as you've heard.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.840
Right now, we will hide
ourselves among the asteroids.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.940
When we find a rock
of an appropriate size...

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.650
...we will tie the ship with
anchors, stop the engine...

00:14:55.650 --> 00:15:00.220
...lay low, evade enemy search, 
and hasten the repairs to our ship.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:00.980
Any questions ?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.010
The ship body has been anchored.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:38.390
Engines have been shut down.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:40.000
Has there been any
enemy movement ?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.190
Since we only have passive sensors,
we may not have accurate information...

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:49.880
...but we had so much distance from the enemy, I doubt our movement was tracked.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.640
The enemy ships, however, are
unmistakably headed in our direction.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.870
That's only logical.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:57.860
The enemy knows
we had five ships.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.940
They must intend to confirm the destruction of our ship.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.810
But even though they may
realize it sooner or later...

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.840
...right now, they've been
deceived by the fake explosion...

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:10.900
...and don't think that confirmation is an immediate task.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.800
So you think the
immediate danger has passed.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.200
Yes, sir.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:20.400
Then I will order you again:
return command authority.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.240
I return command.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.340
The First Officer
will assume command.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.730
Good.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.960
Then, LTJG Musel,
I relieve you of duty.{dismiss you from your post.}

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:37.160
Also, I'm charging you with
committing an act of mutiny...

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:40.160
...and will court-martial you upon
our return to the fortress.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.240
Until then, you will be
confined to quarters.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:43.100
That's all.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.730
Security Chief !

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.600
Yes, sir.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:53.190
Do you pledge allegiance to LTJG Musel personally, or to military regulations ?

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:58.000
To military regulations.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.170
Good.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:01.450
Then detain LTJG Musel.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.930
Confine him to quarters,
under your responsibility.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:06.080
Order acknowledged.

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:23.810
LTJG Shamissoe, I will go take a look at the repair situation in the engine room.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.730
In the meantime,
you assume command.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:26.690
Yes, sir.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.690
Listen, it's only till I return.

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.270
Isn't the First Officer
going overboard ?

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:39.490
In the end, LTJG Musel's
decision was correct.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:41.720
But that's just looking at the result.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:44.860
What the First Officer is concerned
about is the issue of military discipline.

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:48.490
But if we followed discipline
and the First Officer's orders...

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.390
...our ship would have
been sunk, too !

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.200
Lord Reinhard...

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.380
No, this is fine.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:07.940
If you were also confined, there'd be nothing left that we could do.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.870
But I wonder if it's safe to leave
command of the ship to the First Officer.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:17.240
If the engine repairs are completed,
this destroyer can probably escape.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.800
But watch the
First Officer's actions.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.290
He could be an enemy.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.660
I hope I'm just imagining it, but...

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.450
Lord Reinhard...

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.680
I'll leave it to you.{ in charge.}

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.360
Keep watch here.

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.010
Is it that bad ?

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.290
It's not impossible to fix the
engine itself, but it'll take time.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.320
And low speed movement is no good.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:10.130
The variable nozzle
is totally wrecked.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:11.920
In other words,
we can't move ?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:18.480
No, it's not that we can't move, but the nozzle is fixed at a high-speed setting.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:22.030
As it is, it'll take time to go from initial velocity to cruising speed.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:29.540
I heard you were here,
so I came to report.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.960
As per your order,
LTJG Musel has been confined.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:34.890
Very good.
You may go.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.810
Shall I assist with the repairs ?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.500
That'd help.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.240
It'd be faster
with more manpower.

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.120
If the Chief Engineer says so.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:46.740
Yes, sir.

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:51.040
Take a look at the panel over there.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:56.960
Basically, you can think of it as a condition where we can't use the low-speed gear.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.340
It'll help if we can find something to help us accelerate, but...

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.770
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.920
What is it ?

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.550
If you're bringing a report, do it later.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:12.480
Well...

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.730
I thought it might be beneficial to have the First Officer's attention also, but...

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:17.090
What is it ?

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:17.960
Well...

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:22.900
...you may already know this, but my
major at the university was astrophysics...

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:27.800
...so when I'm off duty, I've continued to do astronomical observation as a hobby, but...

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:28.750
Get to the point.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.390
I'm sorry.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:37.440
I mean the main star of this system, Altmuel, is a very unstable, red giant star...

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:40.540
...but as I observed it in
comparison with past data...

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:44.790
...I thought there might be a
cycle to its surface eruptions.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.440
Cycle ?

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.190
Please take a look at this.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:59.660
As you say, it does seem like that, but
what does that have to do with anything ?

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.680
Taking into account the
surface eruption cycle...

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:06.190
...I wonder if we could
use the large-scale starwind...

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.190
...that results from such eruptions to accelerate our ship.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:13.990
In order to take full
advantage of the starwind...

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:17.200
...it's necessary for us to
temporarily get closer to the star.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:19.390
So to deceive
enemy surveillance...

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:23.280
...we'll pretend to be a natural object
and fall toward the star using its gravity.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:30.690
Then by riding the starwind from the star's eruption, we'll aim to escape instantly.

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:34.570
It's only a calculation, but it's possible to
accelerate up to 3 times the usual speed.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.570
Wait a minute.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:40.390
What happens if the eruption
doesn't occur as expected ?

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:45.770
We won't escape the star's gravity, and
we'll fall into the star and burn, won't we ?

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:47.200
That's...

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.580
...exactly what you say.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.750
But the eruption should take place.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:51.820
"Should" ?

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.920
I can't accept such an
uncertain proposition.

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:55.940
But...

00:21:55.940 --> 00:22:00.850
Seaman, though it's okay for you
to pursue your hobby when you're off duty...

00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:02.250
...right now, we're in
an emergency situation.

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:06.300
I'd prefer you to make an
effort to fulfill your given duties.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.250
Go on now and
focus on doing repairs.

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:18.200
Isn't there a more realistic solution ?

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:22.250
If we take time accelerating around here,
it's like urging the enemy to come find us.

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:27.070
Sir, please return to
the bridge immediately.

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:28.200
What happened ?

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:30.000
The situation is unfavorable.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.440
It looks like the enemy
fleet contains carriers.

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.500
Carriers ?

00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:34.670
How many ?

00:22:34.670 --> 00:22:36.180
One ship has been confirmed.

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:39.240
It seems that the reserves from the rear just caught up, but...

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:41.600
This is bad...

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:43.940
If the enemy fighters launch...

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:47.490
...I don't know if we can escape, regardless of whether the engine has been fixed.

00:22:52.340 --> 00:22:55.990
On September 2nd 
of Imperial Year 482...

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:01.510
...Destroyer Hameln II was facing
an extremely desperate situation.

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:03.800
To be continued

